#: ../../li3po4/beta-gamma-comparison.rst:80
msgid ""
"CHGNetの式量当たりの体積は、文献DFT-"
"PBEよりβ相で0.07%、γ相で0.06%大きく、両相でほぼ一致します。格子定数の平均相対誤差の差は、両相とも0.02パーセントポイントです。"
msgstr ""
"The volumes per formula unit from CHGNet are 0.07% larger for the β phase"
" and 0.06% larger for the γ phase than those from DFT-PBE (Li et al.), so"
" the two methods give nearly the same volumes in both phases. The mean "
"relative errors of the lattice constants differ by 0.02 percentage points"
" in both phases."

#: ../../li3po4/beta-gamma-comparison.rst:82
msgid ""
"文献NNPの体積は、文献DFT-PBEよりβ相で0.60%、γ相で2.13%小さく、両相で実験値に近づきます。\\ "
"格子定数の平均相対誤差もβ相で0.96%、γ相で0.62%と、文献DFT-PBEより小さい値です。"
msgstr ""
"The volumes from NNP (Li et al.) are 0.60% smaller for the β phase and "
"2.13% smaller for the γ phase than those from DFT-PBE (Li et al.), "
"bringing both closer to the experimental values. \\ The mean relative "
"errors of the lattice constants are also smaller with NNP (Li et al.): "
"0.96% for the β phase and 0.62% for the γ phase."

#: ../../li3po4/beta-gamma-comparison.rst:85
msgid ""
"OpenMX/PBEの体積は、文献DFT-"
"PBEよりβ相で約1.59%、γ相で約2.15%大きく、実験値からのずれもCHGNetより大きいです。\\ "
"OpenMX/PBEの比較には掲載の格子定数を使いました。差の要因を調べるには、最終構造と最適化条件の確認が必要です。"
msgstr ""
"The volumes from OpenMX/PBE are about 1.59% larger for the β phase and "
"about 2.15% larger for the γ phase than those from DFT-PBE (Li et al.). "
"The OpenMX/PBE volumes also differ more from the experimental values than"
" the CHGNet volumes do. \\ We used the lattice constants listed here for "
"the OpenMX/PBE comparison. Identifying the reasons for the differences "
"requires checking the final structures and optimization conditions."

#: ../../li3po4/beta-gamma-comparison.rst:89
msgid "まとめ"
msgstr "Summary"

#: ../../li3po4/beta-gamma-comparison.rst:91
msgid ""
"CHGNetの格子定数と体積は両相とも文献DFT-PBEの値とほぼ一致し、実験値からのずれも同程度でした。\\ "
"ここで比較したのは、手法や最適化条件が異なる計算で得た格子定数と体積です。\\ "
"相の安定性や拡散の精度を評価するには、相対エネルギーや拡散係数を別途比較する必要があります。"
msgstr ""
"For both phases, the CHGNet lattice constants and volumes agreed closely "
"with DFT-PBE (Li et al.), and the two methods gave similar deviations "
"from the experimental values. \\ We compared lattice constants and "
"volumes obtained with different methods and optimization conditions. \\ "
"Evaluating phase stability or the accuracy of diffusion predictions "
"requires separate comparisons of relative energies or diffusion "
"coefficients."

